WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.702
Good morning, listeners.

2
00:00:03.652 --> 00:00:07.488
Today is October 22, 2026.

3
00:00:07.488 --> 00:00:13.444
Overnight, Wall Street mounted an uneasy relief rally, with tech leading a fragile rebound.

4
00:00:13.444 --> 00:00:22.635
The Nasdaq rose one point zero five percent, the S and P five hundred gained point five percent, and the Dow added point six nine percent.

5
00:00:22.635 --> 00:00:30.576
Crude oil pulled back from intraday highs after reports indicated Persian Gulf flows stabilized, lifting broader risk sentiment.

6
00:00:30.576 --> 00:00:39.351
Ten-year Treasury yields eased slightly, yet hot wholesale inflation and aggressive Federal Reserve rate expectations keep bonds tightly bound.

7
00:00:39.351 --> 00:00:44.768
The consensus view treats this tape as an oversold bounce rather than a structural bottom.

8
00:00:44.768 --> 00:00:51.177
The S and P five hundred remains trapped in a tight band between seventy-six hundred and seventy-eight hundred.

9
00:00:51.177 --> 00:00:56.152
Sustained upside momentum requires clearing seventy-eight hundred convincingly.

10
00:00:56.152 --> 00:01:04.400
Meanwhile, triple Q reclaimed its five-day moving average, but faces a heavy technical ceiling at seven hundred forty-eight dollars.

11
00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:11.079
Corporate buyback blackouts are beginning to thaw, adding passive liquidity that could cushion near-term downside.

12
00:01:11.079 --> 00:01:18.113
However, tech sector liquidity remains under intense scrutiny as institutions continue aggressive de-leveraging.

13
00:01:18.113 --> 00:01:27.304
Semiconductors staged a modest bounce after nine consecutive down sessions, yet credit default swap spreads on major infrastructure players widened.

14
00:01:27.304 --> 00:01:34.008
Heavy AI capital spending has transformed from a growth catalyst into an institutional balance sheet anxiety.

15
00:01:34.008 --> 00:01:42.084
Investors now ruthlessly penalize any company providing conservative guidance or burning cash without immediate monetized returns.

16
00:01:42.084 --> 00:01:51.532
Looking at individual equities, Meta delivered a stellar third quarter, driven by rapid monetization of its artificial intelligence recommendation algorithms.

17
00:01:51.532 --> 00:01:58.383
Revenue hit sixty-four point six billion dollars, and earnings beat expectations by twenty-six cents.

18
00:01:58.383 --> 00:02:05.907
However, quarterly capital expenditures surged to nearly thirty-five billion dollars, pushing free cash flow negative.

19
00:02:05.907 --> 00:02:14.547
Meta shares gained post-market, yet its widening credit default spreads highlight simmering institutional caution around long-term lease commitments.

20
00:02:14.547 --> 00:02:21.275
Tesla presented a mixed fundamental picture, posting flat third-quarter revenue of twenty-eight billion dollars.

21
00:02:21.275 --> 00:02:29.375
Earnings per share slipped four percent year over year to forty-eight cents, while free cash flow reached one point five billion dollars.

22
00:02:29.375 --> 00:02:38.738
Management lowered full-year capital expenditure targets, leaving the stock suspended between electric vehicle margin compression and future robotics optionality.

23
00:02:38.738 --> 00:02:46.741
Super Micro Computer provided unexpected preliminary strength, raising forward gross margin guidance back above twelve percent.

24
00:02:46.741 --> 00:02:54.608
The update triggered a sharp nine point five percent short squeeze, testing key moving average resistance near thirty-two dollars.

25
00:02:54.608 --> 00:02:58.947
Traders should watch twenty-eight dollars as immediate technical support.

26
00:02:58.947 --> 00:03:02.954
That concludes today's XiaoFang Finance Morning Brief.

27
00:03:02.954 --> 00:03:07.121
Thank you for listening, trade safely, and see you tomorrow.
